1
00:00:01,375 --> 00:00:02,710
"Previously on The Mentalist..."

2
00:00:02,835 --> 00:00:06,088
"She told me Red John has a tattoo
on his left shoulder"

3
00:00:06,506 --> 00:00:07,673
"three dots."

4
00:00:08,049 --> 00:00:09,217
That's my leverage.

5
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:13,554
Gather all five suspects together
at the same place, same time

6
00:00:13,679 --> 00:00:15,223
and then start checking
for the tattoo.

7
00:00:15,348 --> 00:00:16,390
How do we do that?

8
00:00:16,516 --> 00:00:18,935
- Meet me at 8:00 on Thursday night.
- Fine.

9
00:00:19,060 --> 00:00:20,520
Thursday night at 8:00.

10
00:00:20,645 --> 00:00:22,855
- I'll need your help.
- Well, then you've got it.

11
00:00:22,980 --> 00:00:25,316
If you don't show up,
he will assume you're Red John.

12
00:00:25,441 --> 00:00:29,737
If I do this, will you and Jane drop
the whole that "I'm Red John" business?

13
00:00:29,862 --> 00:00:31,447
For once and for all.

14
00:00:31,572 --> 00:00:33,574
- You really think you've got him?
- I do.

15
00:00:33,699 --> 00:00:36,619
- I want to be there when you end this.
- I was hoping you'd say that.

16
00:00:36,869 --> 00:00:38,454
Red John.

17
00:00:38,621 --> 00:00:42,250
Nothing would give me more pleasure
than to be with you there tonight.

18
00:00:42,375 --> 00:00:45,670
Red John... has a tattoo.

19
00:00:47,380 --> 00:00:49,382
Three dots on his left arm.

20
00:00:49,924 --> 00:00:53,386
On his shoulder. And you all...

21
00:00:54,679 --> 00:00:55,972
are gonna show me...

22
00:00:58,724 --> 00:00:59,767
now.

23
00:01:04,397 --> 00:01:05,648
Let's go. Come on.

24
00:01:07,316 --> 00:01:08,818
That's it. Take it off.

25
00:01:12,613 --> 00:01:13,656
Nonsense.

26
00:01:22,373 --> 00:01:23,416
Very good.

27
00:01:30,339 --> 00:01:31,549
It's not what you think.

28
00:01:32,550 --> 00:01:33,593
You got it wrong.

29
00:01:34,802 --> 00:01:36,053
I'm not Red John.

30
00:01:37,138 --> 00:01:39,140
Patrick, wait. Patrick!

31
00:01:39,265 --> 00:01:40,308
Look... here.

32
00:01:40,683 --> 00:01:41,726
Look.

33
00:01:59,869 --> 00:02:00,911
On your feet.

34
00:02:01,621 --> 00:02:02,747
Over with those two.

35
00:02:08,377 --> 00:02:09,420
You stay there.

36
00:02:10,504 --> 00:02:11,839
Okay, you three...

37
00:02:12,632 --> 00:02:14,592
Over against that wall...
now.

38
00:02:22,558 --> 00:02:23,768
"Wait! No!"

39
00:02:58,636 --> 00:03:00,054
Call the fire department
and E.M.T.s

40
00:03:00,179 --> 00:03:01,972
let them know that there's
multiple casualties

41
00:03:02,098 --> 00:03:03,474
- and set up a perimeter.
- Yes, ma'am.

42
00:03:03,599 --> 00:03:05,893
- Give me your flashlight. I'm going in.
- Here you go.

43
00:03:11,148 --> 00:03:12,191
Jane.

44
00:03:13,859 --> 00:03:14,985
Jane.

45
00:03:27,665 --> 00:03:28,708
Agent Smith.

46
00:03:28,833 --> 00:03:30,876
Agent Smith, it's Teresa Lisbon.
Are you okay?

47
00:03:31,377 --> 00:03:33,087
- What happened?
- There was an explosion.

48
00:03:33,212 --> 00:03:35,673
The E.M.T.s are on their way.
They're gonna help you.

49
00:03:39,844 --> 00:03:41,262
- Don't move!
- What?

50
00:03:41,387 --> 00:03:44,140
Put your hands in the air,
or I'll shoot! Do it!

51
00:03:44,306 --> 00:03:46,100
Okay, listen, I don't know
what you're talking about.

52
00:03:46,308 --> 00:03:47,727
You're clearly
making a big mistake.

53
00:03:58,946 --> 00:04:00,197
Which way did Smith go?

54
00:04:00,781 --> 00:04:01,991
- Oh, my God, Lisbon.
- Boss!

55
00:04:02,199 --> 00:04:03,909
We have to find Smith.
He's Red John.

56
00:04:04,869 --> 00:04:05,911
I'll get help.

57
00:04:07,913 --> 00:04:08,956
Jane?

58
00:04:10,458 --> 00:04:11,625
Can you hear me?

59
00:04:13,294 --> 00:04:15,713
Jane? Come on.

60
00:04:44,181 --> 00:04:46,016
- You okay?
- I'm fine.

61
00:04:46,433 --> 00:04:49,728
The doctors say Jane's stable.
There's no major trauma or anything.

62
00:04:50,312 --> 00:04:51,563
He's just not awake.

63
00:05:01,615 --> 00:05:02,866
{\an8}They found the remains
of three people.

64
00:05:02,991 --> 00:05:06,203
{\an8}Positive I.D.s for Bret Stiles, Ray Haffner
and Thomas McAllister.

65
00:05:06,328 --> 00:05:09,373
{\an8}Are you sure? I would think Bret Stiles
would survive a nuclear attack.

66
00:05:09,498 --> 00:05:10,874
{\an8}The bodies are all burnt to a crisp

67
00:05:11,291 --> 00:05:13,377
{\an8}but the crime techs
did spot D.N.A. tests.

68
00:05:13,502 --> 00:05:15,379
{\an8}Coroner's office checked it
against medical records.

69
00:05:15,504 --> 00:05:18,006
Stiles, Haffner, and McAllister
are all positively dead.

70
00:05:18,132 --> 00:05:19,800
Uh, what about Smith?
Any sightings?

71
00:05:20,008 --> 00:05:21,593
Not yet. Rigsby and Van Pelt
are on it.

72
00:05:50,372 --> 00:05:51,415
Sir?

73
00:05:51,665 --> 00:05:53,792
- Ah, thought I might find you here.
- Are you all right?

74
00:05:53,917 --> 00:05:56,962
{\an8}Uh, I'm fine. I could use
a cup of coffee, actually.

75
00:05:57,087 --> 00:05:58,130
{\an8}Would you go and get me one?

76
00:05:58,255 --> 00:06:00,090
{\an8}We're just about to coordinate
the manhunt for Smith.

77
00:06:00,215 --> 00:06:01,675
Well, you should just
go and get him.

78
00:06:01,800 --> 00:06:03,844
{\an8}Well, I'd like
to stay here, sir.

79
00:06:04,052 --> 00:06:05,262
{\an8}- Well, are...
- Cho and the team... they can handle it.

80
00:06:05,387 --> 00:06:08,098
- Are you refusing a direct order?
- Well, no.

81
00:06:08,515 --> 00:06:09,558
No, I just want to stay here with him.

82
00:06:09,683 --> 00:06:10,976
Why don't you listen
a little more closely?

83
00:06:11,101 --> 00:06:12,436
{\an8}I am ordering you
to get out there

84
00:06:12,644 --> 00:06:14,062
{\an8}put your team together,
and get Smith.

85
00:06:17,107 --> 00:06:19,234
{\an8}Jane? Jane?
Where's the damn call button?

86
00:06:19,359 --> 00:06:20,569
{\an8}I'll...I'll get the nurse.

87
00:06:22,613 --> 00:06:23,655
{\an8}Jane.

88
00:06:24,531 --> 00:06:25,574
{\an8}Hey.

89
00:06:40,255 --> 00:06:41,298
{\an8}Hey boss.

90
00:07:10,118 --> 00:07:11,787
Our working theory is that Red John
brought in the bomb

91
00:07:11,912 --> 00:07:13,455
to kill Jane and the other suspects.

92
00:07:13,580 --> 00:07:14,623
Okay, but how?

93
00:07:14,748 --> 00:07:16,667
Chances are, Red John
snuck the bomb in on his person.

94
00:07:16,792 --> 00:07:18,335
Crime techs have pulled
fragments of the bomb casings

95
00:07:18,460 --> 00:07:20,546
{\an8}from the walls...
very small fragments.

96
00:07:20,671 --> 00:07:23,298
{\an8}This tells us that the explosive
was dense, high-powered.

97
00:07:23,549 --> 00:07:24,591
{\an8}That doesn't sound homemade.

98
00:07:24,716 --> 00:07:25,843
{\an8}No. Military grade's my bet

99
00:07:26,009 --> 00:07:27,177
{\an8}which means it could be traceable.

100
00:07:27,344 --> 00:07:29,388
{\an8}These are the most likely sources.

101
00:07:30,055 --> 00:07:31,598
{\an8}I want you to check for any recent thefts

102
00:07:31,723 --> 00:07:33,392
- or missing explosives from any of them.
- All right, will do.

103
00:07:33,976 --> 00:07:35,143
- Got something?
- Yeah.

104
00:07:35,269 --> 00:07:37,187
{\an8}Lisbon wounded Smith
before he escaped.

105
00:07:37,312 --> 00:07:38,605
{\an8}He's walking around
with a bullet.

106
00:07:39,189 --> 00:07:40,732
{\an8}Oh. Well, hospitals have
to declare gunshot wounds

107
00:07:40,858 --> 00:07:42,150
{\an8}so he can't go to an E.R.

108
00:07:42,276 --> 00:07:44,570
{\an8}Right, so he needs a doctor
who'll keep quiet.

109
00:07:44,945 --> 00:07:46,196
{\an8}Smith's based
here in Sacramento

110
00:07:46,321 --> 00:07:48,824
so I looked into some of his
old cases around town.

111
00:07:48,949 --> 00:07:50,409
He was part of a task force
that arrested

112
00:07:50,534 --> 00:07:52,786
{\an8}Dr. Alek Lavrov last year
in south Sac.

113
00:07:53,203 --> 00:07:55,747
{\an8}A Dr. Feelgood writing
illegal oxycontin scripts.

114
00:07:55,873 --> 00:07:57,666
{\an8}- So?
- So the case went bad

115
00:07:57,791 --> 00:07:59,585
{\an8}evidence was lost,
and Lavrov walked.

116
00:07:59,710 --> 00:08:01,169
So Smith knows exactly
where to find a doctor

117
00:08:01,295 --> 00:08:03,630
who won't talk to the cops.
Great, let's go check it out.

118
00:08:13,932 --> 00:08:15,309
- It's not what you think.
- No?

119
00:08:15,642 --> 00:08:16,685
I'm not Red John.

120
00:08:16,810 --> 00:08:18,478
Patrick, wait. Look.

121
00:08:34,828 --> 00:08:35,996
Welcome back.

122
00:08:43,545 --> 00:08:44,588
Lisbon.

123
00:08:46,048 --> 00:08:47,966
There was an explosion
at your house.

124
00:08:49,217 --> 00:08:51,845
- How long have I been out?
- 12 hours.

125
00:08:53,889 --> 00:08:57,601
Reede Smith is Red John.
I saw the tattoo on his shoulder.

126
00:08:58,560 --> 00:08:59,978
He's not the only one.

127
00:09:00,854 --> 00:09:02,689
McAllister has one, too.

128
00:09:02,814 --> 00:09:05,776
He's dead.
So are Stiles and Haffner.

129
00:09:06,026 --> 00:09:07,945
- And Bertram.
- Bertram?

130
00:09:08,737 --> 00:09:11,823
- He has the tattoo as well.
- Oh, my God.

131
00:09:12,699 --> 00:09:14,034
He was just here.

132
00:09:14,701 --> 00:09:15,744
He was standing over you.

133
00:09:15,869 --> 00:09:17,287
He...he was trying
to get me to leave.

134
00:09:17,412 --> 00:09:18,455
He was gonna kill you.

135
00:09:18,580 --> 00:09:20,707
- Where are my clothes?
- Slow down, okay?

136
00:09:20,874 --> 00:09:22,084
- Just...
- No, it's okay. We don't have time.

137
00:09:22,209 --> 00:09:24,336
- Jane. Jane.
- Where are my clothes?

138
00:09:27,422 --> 00:09:28,507
This is Teresa Lisbon.

139
00:09:28,632 --> 00:09:30,467
Put out a statewide alert
for the apprehension

140
00:09:30,592 --> 00:09:32,344
of Reede Smith
and Gail Bertram.

141
00:09:33,261 --> 00:09:34,972
Yes, Director Bertram.

142
00:09:35,806 --> 00:09:37,015
Approach with caution.

143
00:09:37,140 --> 00:09:38,767
They're considered
armed and dangerous.

144
00:09:39,476 --> 00:09:40,936
One of them is Red John.

145
00:09:56,284 --> 00:09:57,327
Oh my God!

146
00:09:57,452 --> 00:09:58,578
Move along, ma'am.
Police business.

147
00:10:01,665 --> 00:10:02,791
God!

148
00:10:05,210 --> 00:10:06,253
Yes.

149
00:10:07,045 --> 00:10:10,632
- The bullet is still inside you.
- No crap! Get it out!

150
00:10:12,509 --> 00:10:13,927
This is going to hurt.

151
00:10:14,886 --> 00:10:16,888
Are you sure you won't
take something for the pain?

152
00:10:17,514 --> 00:10:20,976
No... No. I gotta stay sharp.

153
00:10:21,393 --> 00:10:22,436
As you like.

154
00:10:24,813 --> 00:10:25,856
God!

155
00:10:39,870 --> 00:10:40,912
Tiger, tiger.

156
00:10:41,496 --> 00:10:42,539
Tiger, tiger.

157
00:10:43,498 --> 00:10:44,541
Smith in there?

158
00:10:44,666 --> 00:10:46,293
Yeah. He's screaming
his head off.

159
00:10:46,543 --> 00:10:48,754
He won't be a problem.
How you wanna do it?

160
00:10:48,879 --> 00:10:50,505
I just got word
from inside CBI.

161
00:10:50,630 --> 00:10:53,133
Couple of agents are coming here
right now looking for Smith.

162
00:10:53,258 --> 00:10:54,760
- So what do we do?
- We hurry.

163
00:10:54,885 --> 00:10:57,471
You go get him.
I'll run interference if CBI shows.

164
00:10:57,596 --> 00:10:58,638
You got it.

165
00:10:58,889 --> 00:11:02,059
Hey. Take him out the back.
Do it there.

166
00:11:15,655 --> 00:11:17,574
- He made me do this. I'm innocent.
- Shut up.

167
00:11:17,699 --> 00:11:19,034
I would have called the police
as soon as he left.

168
00:11:19,159 --> 00:11:20,410
- I don't want any trouble!
- Quiet!

169
00:11:24,372 --> 00:11:25,457
You association?

170
00:11:25,707 --> 00:11:27,542
Tiger, tiger.
Why didn't you call us?

171
00:11:27,876 --> 00:11:29,628
Funnily enough,
I got trust issues.

172
00:11:29,836 --> 00:11:31,296
Hey, you gotta trust
your friends.

173
00:11:31,671 --> 00:11:34,257
I'm here to help you.
Can you walk?

174
00:11:34,382 --> 00:11:35,801
I need to sew him up.
He'll bleed.

175
00:11:37,135 --> 00:11:38,178
I can walk.

176
00:11:55,487 --> 00:11:58,198
- Detective Cordero, right?
- Agent Rigsby.

177
00:11:58,740 --> 00:11:59,783
How are ya?

178
00:12:00,325 --> 00:12:02,577
He's, Sac P.D.
worked the Kirkland shooting.

179
00:12:02,744 --> 00:12:04,746
- This is Agent Grace Van Pelt.
- Hi.

180
00:12:05,455 --> 00:12:06,790
What brings you
to south Sac?

181
00:12:06,915 --> 00:12:09,251
- We're chasing up a lead on Reede...
- Reede Smith.

182
00:12:09,376 --> 00:12:12,379
AKA Red John. Looks like we beat you
to the punch.

183
00:12:12,504 --> 00:12:14,339
One of my guys is in there
getting him right now.

184
00:12:14,673 --> 00:12:15,715
You want us to cover
the back?

185
00:12:15,841 --> 00:12:18,009
- No. No, we got it.
- You sure?

186
00:12:18,218 --> 00:12:21,429
Hey, we might not be CBI,
but we know what we're doing.

187
00:12:21,805 --> 00:12:23,473
Okay. Excuse me.

188
00:12:26,768 --> 00:12:27,811
Yep?

189
00:12:27,936 --> 00:12:28,979
Rigsby, where are you?

190
00:12:29,187 --> 00:12:31,356
Outside the doctor's office.
Looks like Smith's inside.

191
00:12:31,731 --> 00:12:33,024
Are there policemen with you?

192
00:12:33,400 --> 00:12:34,526
Yeah. Why?

193
00:12:34,651 --> 00:12:35,735
Okay, listen carefully.

194
00:12:35,861 --> 00:12:38,238
Do not trust anyone
in law enforcement.

195
00:12:38,530 --> 00:12:40,407
Anyone at all.
Do you understand?

196
00:12:40,699 --> 00:12:42,325
You got it. Thanks.

197
00:12:45,537 --> 00:12:47,080
Let's, go take a look
around back.

198
00:12:47,372 --> 00:12:50,375
Wait a minute. Hey!
Where are you going?

199
00:12:51,251 --> 00:12:52,294
Car's back this way.

200
00:12:52,878 --> 00:12:53,920
Everything's taken care of.

201
00:12:54,045 --> 00:12:56,673
We got a safe house nearby,
fresh clothes, a doctor...

202
00:12:56,798 --> 00:12:57,841
A trip out of town.

203
00:12:59,426 --> 00:13:00,677
A safe house, huh?

204
00:13:01,678 --> 00:13:03,346
You know, I said that
to someone once.

205
00:13:03,805 --> 00:13:06,558
Yeah? What happened after that?

206
00:13:08,018 --> 00:13:09,895
I shot him six times
in the back.

207
00:13:12,439 --> 00:13:13,481
Come on.

208
00:13:17,569 --> 00:13:18,612
Damn it.

209
00:13:24,492 --> 00:13:25,535
Drop your weapon!

210
00:13:37,547 --> 00:13:38,590
Stop!

211
00:13:58,985 --> 00:14:01,571
- You all right?
- Yeah! You good?

212
00:14:01,905 --> 00:14:02,948
Yeah.

213
00:14:09,663 --> 00:14:11,122
Smith got away during the fight.

214
00:14:11,248 --> 00:14:12,374
So did the detective.

215
00:14:12,958 --> 00:14:15,877
Boss, they were trying
to kill Smith and us. Why?

216
00:14:16,002 --> 00:14:17,295
- I don't know.
- Check the shoulder.

217
00:14:17,420 --> 00:14:18,463
What?

218
00:14:18,588 --> 00:14:19,631
Ask him to check
the left shoulder.

219
00:14:19,756 --> 00:14:21,591
Have Rigsby take his shirt off
and look at his shoulder.

220
00:14:21,716 --> 00:14:23,551
Lisbon wants you to check
his left shoulder.

221
00:14:29,224 --> 00:14:30,267
What the hell?

222
00:14:30,767 --> 00:14:32,560
He's got it.
He's got the tattoo.

223
00:14:33,311 --> 00:14:34,521
Boss, what's happening?

224
00:14:34,646 --> 00:14:37,148
All right, bring him in
and don't let anybody else get to him.

225
00:14:38,984 --> 00:14:40,026
Bring him in.

226
00:14:51,536 --> 00:14:53,162
What do we know about the cop
who attacked you?

227
00:14:53,288 --> 00:14:55,665
This is the one we caught.
Officer Paul Wiehagen.

228
00:14:55,790 --> 00:14:57,834
Six years on the force.
Exemplary record

229
00:14:57,959 --> 00:15:00,169
a couple of commendations,
no real discipline problems.

230
00:15:00,295 --> 00:15:02,088
What about the other one...
Detective Cordero?

231
00:15:02,213 --> 00:15:04,424
Put a call in to his captain.
Said he called in sick an hour ago.

232
00:15:04,549 --> 00:15:05,717
And still no sign of Bertram.

233
00:15:05,842 --> 00:15:08,636
Let's focus on the one we do have.
Maybe Jane will figure it out.

234
00:15:11,180 --> 00:15:12,432
Did someone send you
to kill Reede Smith?

235
00:15:14,517 --> 00:15:15,601
I got nothing to say.

236
00:15:15,852 --> 00:15:16,936
Why were you gonna
murder him?

237
00:15:21,816 --> 00:15:23,776
What about the tattoo?
What's it mean?

238
00:15:28,072 --> 00:15:30,116
You're not a big talker.
I get it.

239
00:15:30,950 --> 00:15:33,119
Loose lips sink ships
and all that.

240
00:15:33,369 --> 00:15:35,663
The bad news is,
you have a lousy poker face.

241
00:15:36,581 --> 00:15:38,875
So we're gonna play a little
game of show-and-tell.

242
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:41,544
I'm gonna tell you something, and you're
gonna show me with your face

243
00:15:42,420 --> 00:15:43,921
whether I'm right or not.

244
00:15:44,339 --> 00:15:45,423
That sound fun?

245
00:15:47,091 --> 00:15:48,259
You ever steal anything?

246
00:15:50,595 --> 00:15:52,055
Did you ever cheat
on your girlfriend?

247
00:15:53,765 --> 00:15:54,807
Hit her?

248
00:15:55,391 --> 00:15:56,768
Do you like causing pain?

249
00:15:57,143 --> 00:15:58,853
I never hit a woman
in my life.

250
00:15:58,978 --> 00:16:01,064
Do you belong to a secret
organization of cops

251
00:16:01,189 --> 00:16:02,690
and other government officials?

252
00:16:05,193 --> 00:16:06,235
Yes.

253
00:16:06,903 --> 00:16:10,531
You've committed crimes
on behalf of that organization before.

254
00:16:12,992 --> 00:16:14,035
Right?

255
00:16:14,994 --> 00:16:17,789
Agent Smith is a member also...

256
00:16:19,248 --> 00:16:20,291
Right?

257
00:16:21,501 --> 00:16:23,461
The organization sent you
to the doctor's office

258
00:16:23,586 --> 00:16:25,880
to kill him... right?

259
00:16:27,882 --> 00:16:30,718
CBI director Gail Bertram
is also a member.

260
00:16:32,720 --> 00:16:33,805
You don't know.

261
00:16:34,180 --> 00:16:35,932
Too low on the totem pole, huh?

262
00:16:36,724 --> 00:16:39,268
Agent Reede Smith
is Red John.

263
00:16:40,520 --> 00:16:41,562
Don't know.

264
00:16:43,231 --> 00:16:45,149
Gail Bertram's Red John.

265
00:16:47,318 --> 00:16:48,361
Don't know.

266
00:16:49,570 --> 00:16:52,490
That tattoo on your shoulder
is the membership sign.

267
00:16:54,951 --> 00:16:56,369
I don't know
what you're talking about.

268
00:16:56,494 --> 00:16:57,537
Right again.

269
00:17:00,164 --> 00:17:01,332
There's a password, too...

270
00:17:01,457 --> 00:17:04,085
something you say
as a greeting or a...

271
00:17:04,794 --> 00:17:06,087
Distress signal.

272
00:17:08,339 --> 00:17:09,549
"Tiger, tiger".

273
00:17:12,301 --> 00:17:13,761
Get out of my head.

274
00:17:14,470 --> 00:17:18,224
- A secret society of dirty cops.
- And Red John's a member.

275
00:17:19,434 --> 00:17:20,476
Partridge.

276
00:17:20,601 --> 00:17:22,854
He said "tiger, tiger" to me
right before he died.

277
00:17:23,646 --> 00:17:25,148
Yes. Yes.

278
00:17:25,273 --> 00:17:27,066
He was asking for help

279
00:17:27,233 --> 00:17:28,985
in the hopes
that you were a member.

280
00:17:29,277 --> 00:17:30,361
But if he had a tattoo

281
00:17:30,486 --> 00:17:32,071
it would have been
in the autopsy report.

282
00:17:32,196 --> 00:17:34,574
Well, you can't trust a file.
We have to see it.

283
00:17:34,699 --> 00:17:36,492
I'll have Cho track down the body.

284
00:17:36,701 --> 00:17:38,369
But Partridge could be
buried by now.

285
00:17:38,494 --> 00:17:39,871
Well, have Cho bring
a shovel.

286
00:17:40,037 --> 00:17:42,665
The team's looking for Smith,
Bertram's on the run.

287
00:17:42,790 --> 00:17:43,875
So who's Red John?

288
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:45,418
Is it Bertram or Smith?

289
00:17:47,545 --> 00:17:49,213
I need to look them
both in the eye.

290
00:17:51,507 --> 00:17:53,968
Yeah, the coroner released his body,
like, two days ago.

291
00:17:54,093 --> 00:17:56,053
- Murder victim, huh?
- Yeah.

292
00:17:56,471 --> 00:17:58,514
I figured. That's why
we held him for so long.

293
00:17:59,515 --> 00:18:00,808
Good thing you got here today.

294
00:18:01,100 --> 00:18:03,060
Tomorrow there won't be
much left of him to look at.

295
00:18:03,895 --> 00:18:04,937
Here we go.

296
00:18:05,062 --> 00:18:06,105
Brett Partridge.

297
00:18:06,272 --> 00:18:07,315
Give me a hand, huh?

298
00:18:28,377 --> 00:18:29,504
He's all yours.

299
00:18:30,254 --> 00:18:31,297
Give me your knife.

300
00:18:39,597 --> 00:18:40,890
They dress 'em
before we burn 'em.

301
00:18:41,265 --> 00:18:42,308
Don't ask me why.

302
00:18:59,534 --> 00:19:00,576
Cho sent a picture.

303
00:19:06,374 --> 00:19:07,416
What does it mean?

304
00:19:07,750 --> 00:19:08,960
What do you think it means?

305
00:19:16,467 --> 00:19:17,510
What happened with Smith?

306
00:19:18,594 --> 00:19:22,056
We almost got him at his doctor's office.
That CBI team showed up.

307
00:19:22,473 --> 00:19:23,766
Smith's in the wind.

308
00:19:24,058 --> 00:19:25,560
That's a good place to be.

309
00:19:26,769 --> 00:19:28,813
I've got some business in here
so wait for me.

310
00:19:38,864 --> 00:19:40,449
Thank you, Mr. Thomas.

311
00:19:40,616 --> 00:19:43,077
- We haven't seen you for a while.
- Yeah. It's nice to see you.

312
00:20:38,633 --> 00:20:39,759
Smith could be anywhere by now.

313
00:20:39,884 --> 00:20:41,802
I tried to trace the G.P.S.
signal on his cell phone.

314
00:20:41,927 --> 00:20:43,137
It's been dead for hours.

315
00:20:43,304 --> 00:20:45,556
A dirty F.B.I. agent like him
has to have a burner.

316
00:20:45,681 --> 00:20:47,725
Dr. Lavrov says he didn't
get the chance to sew Smith up.

317
00:20:47,850 --> 00:20:49,435
He's still walking around
with a bullet wound.

318
00:20:49,602 --> 00:20:51,354
So he's in a bad way
wherever he is.

319
00:20:51,520 --> 00:20:52,980
He'll get picked up
by someone eventually.

320
00:20:53,105 --> 00:20:54,523
Yeah, but any cop
who finds him...

321
00:21:03,824 --> 00:21:05,701
This is scary.
We can't trust anyone.

322
00:21:07,662 --> 00:21:08,704
Nope.

323
00:21:48,285 --> 00:21:50,538
- Agent Van Pelt.
- You gotta help me.

324
00:21:50,705 --> 00:21:51,747
Agent Smith.

325
00:21:51,997 --> 00:21:54,792
They're gonna kill me.
I wanna surrender.

326
00:21:54,917 --> 00:21:55,960
Where are you?

327
00:21:59,714 --> 00:22:01,716
Downtown.
Call Cho. He should be close.

328
00:22:02,299 --> 00:22:03,342
Okay, we're on our way.

329
00:22:06,387 --> 00:22:07,722
Good. Thank you.

330
00:22:10,683 --> 00:22:12,184
Smith reached out to CBI.

331
00:22:12,476 --> 00:22:14,729
He used the burner
the association gave him.

332
00:22:14,854 --> 00:22:15,896
We were listening.

333
00:22:16,021 --> 00:22:17,982
- He's turning himself in.
- Yeah. Rat.

334
00:22:18,441 --> 00:22:20,317
That CBI team is on its way
to get him now.

335
00:22:20,443 --> 00:22:21,861
Well, we can't have that.
Where is he?

336
00:22:21,986 --> 00:22:24,655
He's in an alley not too far from here.
Our good luck.

337
00:22:24,822 --> 00:22:25,865
Does he know who you are?

338
00:22:25,990 --> 00:22:27,742
Nah, he didn't see me
at the doctor's office.

339
00:22:27,867 --> 00:22:30,077
All right. You are now
a CBI agent.

340
00:22:32,496 --> 00:22:34,123
You want to come along?
Could be fun.

341
00:22:34,623 --> 00:22:36,751
No. I have some other business
to take care of.

342
00:22:36,876 --> 00:22:38,043
- We'll meet up later.
- You got it.

343
00:22:38,169 --> 00:22:39,628
Can you get it right
this time?

344
00:22:41,130 --> 00:22:42,173
Yes sir.

345
00:23:29,860 --> 00:23:31,278
Agent Reede Smith?

346
00:23:32,321 --> 00:23:34,323
You out there?
Agent Van Pelt sent me.

347
00:23:42,247 --> 00:23:43,290
Who are you?

348
00:23:45,876 --> 00:23:48,670
Agent Oscar Cordero, CBI.

349
00:23:49,004 --> 00:23:50,255
I'm here to take you in.

350
00:24:01,516 --> 00:24:02,559
You gotta keep me safe.

351
00:24:03,644 --> 00:24:04,686
They're everywhere.

352
00:24:06,563 --> 00:24:07,648
Yeah.

353
00:24:08,273 --> 00:24:09,316
We are.

354
00:24:11,735 --> 00:24:12,778
God...

355
00:24:12,903 --> 00:24:13,946
Back of the car now.

356
00:24:32,547 --> 00:24:34,841
You didn't really think you
could get away from us, did you?

357
00:24:38,303 --> 00:24:40,347
You're a big boy.
Do me a favor

358
00:24:40,764 --> 00:24:42,182
and get in the trunk
yourself.

359
00:24:42,849 --> 00:24:44,309
Just give me a second,
will you?

360
00:24:44,893 --> 00:24:46,645
You'll have a second
in the trunk.

361
00:24:46,770 --> 00:24:48,814
Now don't make me do
painful things to you.

362
00:24:58,740 --> 00:24:59,783
Get in the car!

363
00:25:12,546 --> 00:25:15,048
I'm gonna need a deal.
Full immunity.

364
00:25:15,382 --> 00:25:16,925
I'm not saying a word
unless I can walk.

365
00:25:17,050 --> 00:25:18,218
So walk.

366
00:25:19,386 --> 00:25:20,429
What?

367
00:25:20,554 --> 00:25:21,805
Get up off your ass
and walk.

368
00:25:22,431 --> 00:25:23,849
But, hey, good luck
getting out of the building

369
00:25:23,974 --> 00:25:25,767
before your friends
catch up with you.

370
00:25:25,892 --> 00:25:27,853
If you tell us
everything we need to know

371
00:25:27,978 --> 00:25:30,272
I promise we will put you
in a federal prison

372
00:25:30,397 --> 00:25:32,107
far away from California.

373
00:25:32,733 --> 00:25:34,276
Someplace
that you'll be safe.

374
00:25:42,617 --> 00:25:44,286
Five years ago,
I hurt my back.

375
00:25:45,579 --> 00:25:47,539
I was helping my cousin
move a stupid couch.

376
00:25:49,124 --> 00:25:50,709
Doctor gave me
some pain pills.

377
00:25:50,834 --> 00:25:52,044
Turns out I liked them.

378
00:25:52,544 --> 00:25:54,296
I got hooked before I even knew
what was happening.

379
00:25:54,421 --> 00:25:57,007
- So?
- So...

380
00:25:59,092 --> 00:26:00,510
I'm chasing a gangbanger
down an alley

381
00:26:00,635 --> 00:26:02,846
in Carson Springs,
and I'm out of it.

382
00:26:03,138 --> 00:26:05,098
I mean, way out of it.

383
00:26:06,433 --> 00:26:08,268
I thought...I thought
I was being followed.

384
00:26:12,814 --> 00:26:13,857
I shot a little girl.

385
00:26:15,567 --> 00:26:16,985
A 12-year-old girl.

386
00:26:20,238 --> 00:26:21,740
Local cops took my blood.

387
00:26:21,865 --> 00:26:23,408
They had witnesses.
They had me cold.

388
00:26:24,743 --> 00:26:25,911
And then this detective

389
00:26:26,745 --> 00:26:28,205
he reaches out to me
and he says

390
00:26:28,663 --> 00:26:30,123
they can make it all
go away.

391
00:26:31,374 --> 00:26:32,417
And they did.

392
00:26:32,542 --> 00:26:35,003
The blood tests,
the witnesses...all of it?

393
00:26:36,338 --> 00:26:37,923
Hell, when they
got done fixing it

394
00:26:38,590 --> 00:26:40,258
the F.B.I. gave me a medal.

395
00:26:43,345 --> 00:26:45,013
And exactly who are "they"?

396
00:26:48,850 --> 00:26:51,144
We call ourselves
the Blake Association.

397
00:26:52,104 --> 00:26:53,146
Why?

398
00:26:53,647 --> 00:26:54,815
"Tiger, tiger."

399
00:26:56,858 --> 00:26:58,652
"Tyger, tyger burning bright"

400
00:27:00,654 --> 00:27:01,947
from the poem by Blake.

401
00:27:04,324 --> 00:27:05,951
Someone's a big fan of his,
I guess.

402
00:27:06,326 --> 00:27:08,036
Well, who else
is in the association?

403
00:27:08,161 --> 00:27:10,122
Cops, judges, F.B.I. agents.

404
00:27:10,247 --> 00:27:12,916
Anyone in law enforcement
that needs a secret covered up.

405
00:27:13,041 --> 00:27:14,334
Like your drug habit.

406
00:27:16,670 --> 00:27:18,046
You need a favor,
you ask for it.

407
00:27:18,255 --> 00:27:20,090
You get asked to do something,
you do it.

408
00:27:20,215 --> 00:27:21,424
"Tiger, tiger."

409
00:27:23,009 --> 00:27:24,052
Yep.

410
00:27:24,719 --> 00:27:26,179
Well, is there somebody
who's in charge?

411
00:27:28,098 --> 00:27:29,141
Must be.

412
00:27:29,850 --> 00:27:31,017
But I don't know who.

413
00:27:31,643 --> 00:27:33,895
I just know my little group.
That's it.

414
00:27:35,564 --> 00:27:36,606
But I'm guessing

415
00:27:37,649 --> 00:27:39,401
there must be hundreds of us,
maybe thousands.

416
00:27:39,526 --> 00:27:41,194
And nobody knows about it?

417
00:27:43,363 --> 00:27:45,323
Bob Kirkland knew about it,
didn't he?

418
00:27:48,743 --> 00:27:51,413
Go ahead, just say it.
Unburden yourself.

419
00:27:54,291 --> 00:27:55,333
Yeah.

420
00:27:56,001 --> 00:27:57,043
He knew too much.

421
00:27:58,086 --> 00:27:59,129
So I killed him.

422
00:28:01,965 --> 00:28:05,051
Do you know that Red John's a member
of the Blake Association?

423
00:28:16,646 --> 00:28:17,689
Are you sure?

424
00:28:18,899 --> 00:28:20,025
Red John had a follower.

425
00:28:21,234 --> 00:28:22,485
Rebecca Anderson.

426
00:28:23,653 --> 00:28:25,363
"Killed some of your guys
about four years ago."

427
00:28:25,488 --> 00:28:27,157
"Yeah, Sam Bosco
and his team."

428
00:28:27,282 --> 00:28:28,325
"Them."

429
00:28:29,534 --> 00:28:31,995
"Someone asked me to get
F.B.I. credentials"

430
00:28:32,120 --> 00:28:34,206
"so that they could access CBI."

431
00:28:36,750 --> 00:28:38,793
Red John or someone
who worked for him

432
00:28:38,919 --> 00:28:41,713
snuck into the CBI
and poisoned Rebecca.

433
00:28:42,631 --> 00:28:43,757
"And you helped them?"

434
00:28:44,633 --> 00:28:46,218
I mean, that's when I knew.

435
00:28:46,343 --> 00:28:49,346
I'd...I'd done a favor
for a serial killer.

436
00:28:50,472 --> 00:28:52,224
Who asked you to get
the credentials?

437
00:28:53,642 --> 00:28:54,935
I don't know.
It was a phone call.

438
00:28:55,268 --> 00:28:57,187
That's the way
the association works.

439
00:28:57,312 --> 00:28:58,355
You never know.

440
00:29:03,526 --> 00:29:04,569
You...

441
00:29:04,694 --> 00:29:06,363
You're gonna be able
to keep me safe, right?

442
00:29:06,488 --> 00:29:07,530
That depends.

443
00:29:09,407 --> 00:29:11,368
Did you murder
my wife and daughter?

444
00:29:15,580 --> 00:29:18,333
I did not murder
your wife and daughter.

445
00:29:20,543 --> 00:29:21,753
I swear on my mother.

446
00:29:31,471 --> 00:29:32,514
Do you believe him?

447
00:29:32,931 --> 00:29:33,974
He confessed to murder.

448
00:29:34,099 --> 00:29:36,518
Red John would never break
like that, not even as an act.

449
00:29:36,643 --> 00:29:39,271
- Well, if Smith isn't Red John...
- That means we have work to do.

450
00:29:39,521 --> 00:29:41,648
And we need help.
Who took over from Brenda Shettrick?

451
00:29:41,773 --> 00:29:43,316
In media relations? Why?

452
00:29:44,025 --> 00:29:45,819
Thank you for coming
on such short notice.

453
00:29:45,944 --> 00:29:48,363
We have CBI consultant
Patrick Jane here

454
00:29:48,738 --> 00:29:51,908
who is here to report a development
in the Red John case.

455
00:29:54,786 --> 00:29:55,829
Thank you.

456
00:29:56,705 --> 00:29:59,499
Ten years ago
the serial killer known as Red John

457
00:29:59,624 --> 00:30:01,251
killed my wife and daughter.

458
00:30:01,501 --> 00:30:05,422
Uh, we've been hunting him
diligently ever since.

459
00:30:06,047 --> 00:30:07,465
Today we're pleased
to announce

460
00:30:07,590 --> 00:30:10,719
that we...we finally have
a name, a face.

461
00:30:11,845 --> 00:30:13,972
The director of the division
of law enforcement

462
00:30:14,097 --> 00:30:16,433
Gail Bertram, is Red John.

463
00:30:18,143 --> 00:30:19,644
He's armed and dangerous.

464
00:30:19,769 --> 00:30:22,355
If you see him,
do not approach him.

465
00:30:22,981 --> 00:30:25,984
Call the California
Bureau of Investigation at once.

466
00:30:26,651 --> 00:30:27,694
Thank you.

467
00:30:35,577 --> 00:30:36,953
One question at a time.

468
00:30:43,858 --> 00:30:44,901
Excuse me ma'am.

469
00:30:49,380 --> 00:30:50,548
So are we gonna talk
about this?

470
00:30:51,424 --> 00:30:52,467
Talk about what?

471
00:30:52,592 --> 00:30:53,885
Bertram is Red John.

472
00:30:54,719 --> 00:30:55,762
Looks like.

473
00:30:57,305 --> 00:30:58,848
And if Jane finds him,
he's gonna kill him.

474
00:30:59,140 --> 00:31:00,183
Yeah.

475
00:31:00,558 --> 00:31:03,269
And we're good with that?
Killing the boss?

476
00:31:03,853 --> 00:31:05,063
- I am.
- Yeah.

477
00:31:06,564 --> 00:31:07,607
Okay.

478
00:31:07,857 --> 00:31:09,567
Just as long as we're
on the same page.

479
00:31:10,151 --> 00:31:11,277
It's just weird, is all.

480
00:31:21,037 --> 00:31:22,163
Does Bertram smoke?

481
00:31:22,705 --> 00:31:23,915
No, I don't think so.

482
00:31:24,374 --> 00:31:25,917
People get them
as gifts sometimes.

483
00:31:34,759 --> 00:31:35,802
Van Pelt.

484
00:31:41,015 --> 00:31:42,058
A flash drive.

485
00:31:42,183 --> 00:31:43,226
Let's take a look.

486
00:31:44,227 --> 00:31:46,979
There's only one file on the drive.
It's password-protected.

487
00:31:47,105 --> 00:31:48,439
I'll have to brute-force it.

488
00:31:48,981 --> 00:31:51,317
Cool. I've been wanting to use
my new F.P.G.A.

489
00:31:51,859 --> 00:31:54,695
- Your what?
- Trust me, don't ask.

490
00:31:57,615 --> 00:31:59,659
And...

491
00:32:00,243 --> 00:32:01,327
We're in.

492
00:32:05,456 --> 00:32:06,499
Crap.

493
00:32:06,624 --> 00:32:07,667
It looks like a list.

494
00:32:07,792 --> 00:32:10,002
Names, maybe?
Can you decode it?

495
00:32:10,128 --> 00:32:11,504
I can try a few things...

496
00:32:11,629 --> 00:32:13,548
but decoding is Jane's
department.

497
00:32:13,714 --> 00:32:14,757
I'll send it to him.

498
00:32:20,179 --> 00:32:22,140
Here you go.
This one isn't messing around.

499
00:32:22,640 --> 00:32:23,683
Lots of peat.

500
00:32:30,148 --> 00:32:31,858
Yeah, that's pretty good.
Can you put some rocks in it?

501
00:32:31,983 --> 00:32:34,026
Are you sure?
This is some fine scotch.

502
00:32:36,237 --> 00:32:37,280
Yeah, I'm sure.

503
00:32:49,250 --> 00:32:50,585
That guy looks like you.

504
00:33:26,704 --> 00:33:27,747
I need a ride.

505
00:33:35,087 --> 00:33:36,172
We're on route
to the bar now.

506
00:33:36,297 --> 00:33:37,924
Highway patrol
shut down the freeways

507
00:33:38,049 --> 00:33:40,551
so if he runs, we've got him,
but what if he hides?

508
00:33:40,676 --> 00:33:42,553
Bertram killed the bartender
in Citrus Heights.

509
00:33:42,678 --> 00:33:44,055
He's got an aunt
with a house there.

510
00:33:44,263 --> 00:33:45,348
You think that's
where he is?

511
00:33:45,723 --> 00:33:47,892
She moved into a retirement home
about six months ago

512
00:33:48,017 --> 00:33:49,185
so her place is empty now.

513
00:33:49,477 --> 00:33:51,521
Sounds like a good place to hide.
What's the address?

514
00:33:51,646 --> 00:33:53,439
1408 Rosemary Street.

515
00:33:53,564 --> 00:33:55,858
We're on our way.
Get Cho and R.R.T. there now

516
00:33:55,983 --> 00:33:57,026
and let the choppers know.

517
00:34:13,292 --> 00:34:15,044
- Is he here?
- If he is. He's in there.

518
00:34:15,169 --> 00:34:17,171
I got Karl and a few guys in the back.
He's not going anywhere.

519
00:34:17,296 --> 00:34:18,339
Do we trust them?

520
00:34:18,464 --> 00:34:20,174
I asked to see their shoulders
no tattoos.

521
00:34:23,594 --> 00:34:26,264
What are you doing here?
I didn't call Sac P.D. S.W.A.T.

522
00:34:26,389 --> 00:34:27,557
Well, someone asked for us.

523
00:34:27,682 --> 00:34:29,433
Let's set up a command center
right here!

524
00:34:29,892 --> 00:34:31,435
Listen, everybody,
I'm in charge!

525
00:34:31,561 --> 00:34:33,688
Different order and district
that's way across town.

526
00:34:33,813 --> 00:34:35,231
What the hell is going on?

527
00:34:36,607 --> 00:34:38,693
He did it.
He called them in.

528
00:34:38,818 --> 00:34:41,404
Well, why would Bertram call
S.W.A.T. to his own location?

529
00:34:41,571 --> 00:34:44,782
He didn't call in one S.W.A.T. team.
He called all of them in.

530
00:34:46,158 --> 00:34:47,201
This is a madhouse.

531
00:34:47,326 --> 00:34:48,494
There's a whole 'nother unit
setting up out back.

532
00:34:48,619 --> 00:34:49,870
We've lost control
of the scene, boss.

533
00:34:49,996 --> 00:34:52,832
He's one of them.
Bertram is one of them.

534
00:34:53,916 --> 00:34:55,167
We gotta shut it down.

535
00:34:58,337 --> 00:34:59,547
Nobody leaves!

536
00:35:00,298 --> 00:35:01,424
No one leaves!

537
00:35:39,086 --> 00:35:40,129
You're clear.

538
00:35:44,508 --> 00:35:45,551
Yeah...

539
00:35:46,969 --> 00:35:48,387
I need something to eat.

540
00:35:48,596 --> 00:35:50,640
How about Chinese?
I know a great place.

541
00:35:51,807 --> 00:35:52,975
Yeah, sounds good.

542
00:35:58,606 --> 00:36:00,191
They found Bertram's clothes
inside the house.

543
00:36:00,316 --> 00:36:01,984
Looks like someone planted
a S.W.A.T. team outfit

544
00:36:02,109 --> 00:36:03,152
in the house
before he got there.

545
00:36:03,277 --> 00:36:06,030
And then called every S.W.A.T.
and R.R.T. in the area.

546
00:36:06,155 --> 00:36:07,865
Any leads about who made
all those calls?

547
00:36:07,990 --> 00:36:09,659
Somebody who could pull
a lot of strings at once.

548
00:36:09,825 --> 00:36:11,077
Blake Association.

549
00:36:12,662 --> 00:36:13,704
Boss.

550
00:36:13,871 --> 00:36:15,873
May I have your attention, please?

551
00:36:16,248 --> 00:36:19,085
Put down your phones
and step away from your desks.

552
00:36:19,960 --> 00:36:21,003
Now.

553
00:36:21,128 --> 00:36:23,422
I'm Special Agent in charge
Teresa Lisbon.

554
00:36:23,839 --> 00:36:24,965
Who the hell are you?

555
00:36:25,341 --> 00:36:27,802
F.B.I. supervisory
Agent Dennis Abbott.

556
00:36:30,054 --> 00:36:32,431
Now I repeat, stand up

557
00:36:32,556 --> 00:36:34,183
and stand away
from your desks...

558
00:36:35,810 --> 00:36:36,936
Please.

559
00:36:37,311 --> 00:36:40,189
We're in the middle of a manhunt
for a dangerous fugitive.

560
00:36:40,314 --> 00:36:41,982
Now if you would like
to assist...

561
00:36:42,108 --> 00:36:45,319
The head of this alleged
law enforcement organization

562
00:36:45,444 --> 00:36:46,612
is a murderer

563
00:36:46,946 --> 00:36:49,740
and a member of a massive
criminal conspiracy.

564
00:36:49,865 --> 00:36:53,035
Which included F.B.I. agents.

565
00:36:53,160 --> 00:36:54,745
Yes, and that's why the bureau
sent me here

566
00:36:54,870 --> 00:36:56,622
from the Austin, Texas, office.

567
00:36:57,081 --> 00:36:58,332
To clean up the mess.

568
00:37:02,753 --> 00:37:07,717
I am holding in my hand
a writ from a federal judge.

569
00:37:08,634 --> 00:37:12,221
The F.B.I.'s closing down
your organization right now.

570
00:37:13,723 --> 00:37:14,849
All of you

571
00:37:15,599 --> 00:37:19,311
are relieved from your active duties
as of this moment.

572
00:37:19,437 --> 00:37:20,688
You can't do that.

573
00:37:22,481 --> 00:37:23,941
I'm here to collect evidence.

574
00:37:24,567 --> 00:37:25,609
Don't get in my way.

575
00:37:25,735 --> 00:37:27,153
Let's go to work, fellas.

576
00:37:40,750 --> 00:37:42,501
"Alright, alright take it easy man"

577
00:37:45,045 --> 00:37:46,964
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.
What's going on here?

578
00:37:47,506 --> 00:37:48,549
That's yours.

579
00:37:52,762 --> 00:37:55,514
Dennis Abbott, F.B.I.
you must be Patrick Jane.

580
00:37:55,639 --> 00:37:56,724
They've shut us down.

581
00:37:56,849 --> 00:37:59,435
We're gonna need to interview you
at some point but it can wait.

582
00:37:59,560 --> 00:38:00,644
We're gonna be here for some time.

583
00:38:00,770 --> 00:38:02,146
Just don't leave town.

584
00:38:03,856 --> 00:38:06,984
- We have a killer to catch.
- Oh, well, that's our problem now.

585
00:38:07,109 --> 00:38:09,028
You had your chance to catch him
and you blew it...

586
00:38:09,153 --> 00:38:10,321
if you were really trying.

587
00:38:20,915 --> 00:38:22,208
That was my favorite cup.

588
00:38:25,377 --> 00:38:26,420
Yeah.

589
00:38:27,046 --> 00:38:29,590
Okay, well, you see
in the funny pages.

590
00:38:35,679 --> 00:38:36,722
What now?

591
00:38:37,890 --> 00:38:38,933
I don't know.

592
00:38:39,099 --> 00:38:41,685
Van Pelt found some coded files
in Bertram's flash drive.

593
00:38:41,811 --> 00:38:42,853
Should we get started
on those?

594
00:38:42,978 --> 00:38:45,397
No, it's a waste of time.
We're done.

595
00:38:45,731 --> 00:38:47,107
There's nothing more
to do here.

596
00:38:48,567 --> 00:38:50,277
Just go home, get some rest.

597
00:38:51,028 --> 00:38:53,531
You're not quitting.
I don't believe it.

598
00:38:54,907 --> 00:38:56,450
No, I'm not quitting.

599
00:38:59,161 --> 00:39:00,204
I'm letting go.

600
00:39:02,832 --> 00:39:04,208
It's out of our hands
for now.

601
00:39:04,917 --> 00:39:06,961
But I'll be in touch.
Okay?

602
00:39:09,129 --> 00:39:11,340
I'm sorry. For everything.


